      "goal_complete": false,
      "qualification": "Source308 removes the native-function RecordKind and persistent descriptor/name/C-name maps in favor of the actual 88-byte GNU-layout subr. It carries the checked decoder repair, exact C-name termination and byte printing, and the command/completion/substitution/property consumers. Six new controls retain actual GNU answers; the original dabbrev failure is fixed without changing its test. All source305/306/307 failures and source308 development negatives remain preserved. The temporary trace test has been removed. Formal selected validation, physical accounting, public ownership, unit reclamation and performance remain separate requirements."
    },
    "goal_complete": false,
    "qualification": "The development control closes the unchanged dabbrev regression and passes6 focused storage/GC/ABI/actual-GNU controls. Its failed predecessors remain preserved. Source308 fixes command recognition and native function identity in text properties and reader substitution, and C-name byte callbacks. No original frozen fixture, expected outcome or audit deviation changed. The temporary diagnostic test was removed. This archive certifies portable code and the closed development run only, not the ongoing gate/release selection, ordinary comparisons, platform validation or performance. Development1 reconstructs by applying its delta after the complete307 patch; development2 adds the trace-test delta. Their complete manifests identify every input."
